"""Approximate strong responses to the letter d, would, and its 'd contraction.

An isolated d in notation is stronger than a d continuing a word. Percent
formatting and LaTeX roman notation boost it further. Would and 'd are
stronger after personal pronouns. Punctuation-attached d, capital D,
Cyrillic д, repeated d, and roman-font commands get smaller responses.
Other tokens get zero. Remember the previous token and 64 text characters,
resetting at document boundaries; no model activations are read.
