The component turns on for words meaning "covering the whole world or the whole nation":
global (any spelling, and 全球 / 全国 in Chinese) gives the strongest response (~5), then
worldwide / nationwide (~3), then world, national, international, universal, throughout,
across, everywhere (~1). "all" gives a weaker response (~0.75). It also responds to "of" after
a quantifier ("one of" ~1.1; "all of", "some of", "each of" ~0.6). A few tool/code identifiers
such as "_editor" and "Reader" get a small negative value. Everything else predicts 0.
The program is stateless: it reads the newest token and the one before it (reset at a
document boundary).
